n the 80s and 90s and and  that we're facing all over again right  at this time and it's a real tribute to  to Steve's book that it received a  wonderful review by somebody who I dare  say is a lot more conservative then  Steve is yesterday in The New York Times  a great a review by Bob Samuelson which  pointed out what a fair-minded and and  and fun to read book it is which it is  so um thank you very much Steve and  congratulations to you and the books are  for sale in the front of the store and  you're watching book TV 48 hours of  nonfiction books coming up at midnight  Eastern a look at the influence of  Wahhabi Islam and its ties to the Saudi  royal family with Stephen Schwartz  author of the two faces of Islam then  meditations of Marcus Aurelius with  translator Gregory Hays Sunday night  Robert Remini profiles Mormon Church  founder Joseph Smith after that on  public lives a panel featuring  biographers Robert Kira
 

